# PHASE 7 — PERSONALIZED PRODUCT RECOMMENDATION ENGINE

Implement or verify a genuine personalized recommendation system.

The system should prioritize products that are relevant to each individual user.

## 7.1 Behavioral signals

Use relevant and lawfully collected signals:

- Product views.
- Repeated product views.
- Search queries.
- Search result clicks.
- Category browsing.
- Successful orders.
- Recent purchase history.
- Relevant product interactions.

Do not treat every interaction equally.

A successful purchase is a stronger interest signal than an accidental view.

A single search must not permanently dominate recommendations.

## 7.2 Recommendation ranking

Build a transparent relevance-scoring mechanism using:

- Category similarity.
- Search intent similarity.
- Product attribute similarity.
- Purchase history.
- Browsing history.
- Recency.
- Product availability.
- Catalog quality.

Apply appropriate time decay.

Exclude:

- Deleted products.
- Unpublished products.
- Ineligible products.
- The current product from its own related-product list.

Do not recommend products that cannot be purchased.

## 7.3 New users and guests

For users without sufficient history:

- Use current product context.
- Use current browsing session.
- Use relevant category signals.
- Use sensible popular-product fallback.

Do not display an empty recommendation section merely because a user has no account.

## 7.4 Privacy and data isolation

- Users must not access other users' private activity history.
- Validate user identity server-side.
- Use appropriate retention rules.
- Do not record passwords or payment credentials.
- Do not collect unnecessary personal information.

